1
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:07,560
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

2
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:12,980
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

3
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:22,860
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

4
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:25,540
nezumiiro no sora no shita

5
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:31,840
Higawari no chizu
ikutsumo no yume ga nijinde ita

6
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:37,960
Itsuka wa sa chippoke na
boku no kono hohaba demo

7
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:44,040
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

8
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:50,200
Tsuyogatte kizutsuita kokoro sukashita you ni

9
00:00:50,340 --> 00:00:57,080
Furidashita amatsubutachi ga
ranhansha kurikaesu

10
00:00:57,260 --> 00:01:02,620
Massugu na hikari ga kousa shite

11
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:09,340
Yukusaki mo tsugenu mama
dokomademo tsukinukeru

12
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:15,100
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakistukete

13
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:21,300
Kono sora no shita donna toko ni ite mo

14
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:28,120
Todoku hazu nanda mada minu sekai e

15
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:39,200
Scar had once again
made an appearance in Central.

16
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:43,520
Ed and Al worked with Ling to
draw the murderous Ishvalan's attention,

17
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:45,860
In an effort to lure out the Homunculi.

18
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:51,220
Their strategy paid off.

19
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:54,640
Before long, the Homunculi
Wrath and Gluttony appeared.

20
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:56,540
However...

21
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:59,100
[SCREAMS]

22
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:01,100
No! Lan Fan!

23
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:08,080
Clever.

24
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:11,000
You took a swipe at me with your kunai.

25
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:13,000
Can I eat her now?

26
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,220
Just make it quick.

27
00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:26,000
Lan Fan, please stay with me!

28
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:32,560
If you thought you could
escape from me that easily,

29
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:35,480
I'm afraid you'll find
you're surely mistaken!

30
00:02:40,140 --> 00:02:42,000
I see you're no stranger to combat.

31
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:44,160
Ugh!

32
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:49,580
All this jumping around,
he's trying to stay in my blind spot.

33
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:52,420
Gluttony!

34
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:07,000
Excellent.
We should have some privacy in here.

35
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:10,000
If you don't mind,
I have some questions.

36
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:13,880
First, I'd like to know who you people are,

37
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:16,500
and how you found out
what's inside Gluttony.

38
00:03:18,220 --> 00:03:20,500
You're looking for an escape? Even now?

39
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:22,000
You don't give up, do you?

40
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:25,920
You might stand a fair chance of getting
away if you'd only abandon the injured girl

41
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:28,640
because she's just excess
baggage at this point.

42
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,700
Excess baggage?

43
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:34,140
I can see all those stars on your uniform.

44
00:03:34,140 --> 00:03:35,460
You're the ruler here.

45
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:38,240
Führer King Bradley, unless I'm mistaken.

46
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:41,000
A ruler's duty is to his people.

47
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,360
Without them, he is no king at all!

48
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:47,360
King Bradley, you're no true king.

49
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:49,000
Not now or ever!

50
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:50,500
Naive boy.

51
00:03:51,140 --> 00:03:55,000
Don't you understand that there
are no true kings in this world?

52
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:58,920
[EXPLOSION]
[BRADLEY GROANS]

53
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
That oughtta hold him.

54
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:05,000
Judging by the draft, there's the exit.

55
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:10,740
Nice try.

56
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:14,320
But your flash bomb didn't
succeed in blinding this eye.

57
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:16,120
[GASPS]

58
00:04:22,620 --> 00:04:23,520
Winry.

59
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:27,000
We won't be away too long.

60
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,680
You be a good little girl, okay?

61
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:30,480
Take care of things while we're gone.

62
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:47,780
Winry?

63
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:50,960
Huh?

64
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:53,260
Here we are.

65
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:25,640
Watching Mr. Hughes leave that day
was like the last time I saw Mom and Dad.

66
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:28,380
Just their backs as they walked away.

67
00:05:29,160 --> 00:05:31,920
You'll come and visit
once in a while, won't you?

68
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:38,560
After all, we wouldn't want
him to get lonesome here.

69
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:41,680
Yes, of course I will.

70
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:09,500
I hear the Elrics are wreaking havoc.

71
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:11,000
What? Again?

72
00:06:11,540 --> 00:06:14,000
The MPs have been
running around like crazy.

73
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:17,300
They're in another fight?

74
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:19,000
Good grief.

75
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,200
It seems they're after that guy
who's been killing off state alchemists.

76
00:06:22,540 --> 00:06:24,480
Seriously? They haven't caught him yet?

77
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:26,760
What is the military waiting for?

78
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:35,000
No. Not again, please!

79
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:39,640
Ah!

80
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,360
It's a dead end!

81
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:54,420
Damn! What now?!

82
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:09,400
Nice one, brother!
Appreciate it!

83
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:11,420
We need to get out of here now!

84
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:12,700
Permission to fire?

85
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:13,400
Not yet.

86
00:07:13,420 --> 00:07:15,060
Why the hell not?

87
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:25,700
Ling hasn't fired the signal flare yet.

88
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:27,700
And brother's getting tired.

89
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
I have to buy us some time.

90
00:07:31,660 --> 00:07:32,640
Scar!

91
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:35,500
You say you believe that
alchemists have defied God.

92
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:37,200
Isn't that hypocritical?

93
00:07:37,420 --> 00:07:39,320
You use alchemy just like we do.

94
00:07:39,740 --> 00:07:42,040
I explained it when we met in East City.

95
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:43,040
It's balance.

96
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:45,500
Where there are creators,
there must be a destroyer.

97
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:46,840
That's a lie!

98
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:52,020
You're using the name of
your god to justify murder!

99
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:54,240
Revenge is all you care about.

100
00:07:55,780 --> 00:07:58,280
When you killed Shou Tucker and Nina...

101
00:07:58,440 --> 00:08:02,040
I suppose you believe you
were doing God's work then, too!

102
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:03,340
Interesting.

103
00:08:03,940 --> 00:08:06,980
You two saw that abomination
as well, did you?

104
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:09,900
Alchemy created that tragic creature.

105
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:14,220
So that's the science you
would spend your lives following?

106
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:16,300
Look at your brother!

107
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:19,640
He's the result of messing
around with somebody's life!

108
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:23,500
That chimera was made
because a man thought he could

109
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:26,500
create when creation is
the province of God alone.

110
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:27,500
[GASP]

111
00:08:27,820 --> 00:08:29,080
Maybe you're right.

112
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,700
But why did you have to kill her?

113
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:33,220
You stole what little life she had left!

114
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:36,620
Foolish as you are, you must
still have known that chimera...

115
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:38,500
could never have returned
to her human state.

116
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,440
[GASPS]

117
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:45,020
It would have lived out its
life as a laboratory specimen.

118
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:49,760
Treated as a test subject,
but never again as a human being.

119
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:56,540
He's right.

120
00:08:57,260 --> 00:09:01,160
Even then, we knew that Nina
would be sent off to live in a laboratory.

121
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:04,320
We knew full well what would happen to her.

122
00:09:04,980 --> 00:09:06,560
We didn't wanna think about it.

123
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:08,480
We knew there was no hope.

124
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:10,500
So we did nothing.

125
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:12,260
Nothing.

126
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:15,040
[FOOTSTEPS]

127
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:29,840
It's true. State Alchemists have
made some serious mistakes

128
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:32,780
But despite what you think,

129
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,740
that doesn't make
what you're doing right.

130
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:36,340
And we can't let you continue!

131
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:41,500
You're so self-righteous.

132
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:45,020
But do you remember two
Amestrian doctors named Rockbell?

133
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:49,580
The order came down
to end the uprising and

134
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:51,840
exterminate Ishval,
but that didn't stop them.

135
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:54,680
They kept right on helping your people!

136
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,020
Wait, brother!

137
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:58,360
Don't you remember them?

138
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:01,500
Those doctors saved your
life, and you killed them!

139
00:10:05,620 --> 00:10:06,640
Brother!

140
00:10:11,140 --> 00:10:12,780
What are you talking about, Ed?

141
00:10:13,860 --> 00:10:15,020
Winry, I...

142
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:20,120
You mean he's the man...
who killed them?

143
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:21,920
My parents?

144
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:23,880
He killed them?

145
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:27,080
What's worse...

146
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:29,040
They helped save you...

147
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:31,340
And you killed them.

148
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:37,320
Why did you?

149
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:40,200
They were my mom and dad.

150
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:41,880
What did they ever do to you?

151
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:44,460
They were doctors.

152
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:46,220
They helped people.

153
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:48,460
They didn't deserve to die!

154
00:10:48,860 --> 00:10:49,860
[SOBS]

155
00:10:50,820 --> 00:10:52,040
Give them back!

156
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:56,000
Give me back my mom and dad, you monster!

157
00:10:56,580 --> 00:10:58,800
[SOBBING]

158
00:11:08,060 --> 00:11:10,120
Winry, hold on...

159
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:11,500
You can't.

160
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:13,040
Don't do this.

161
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:14,100
Winry!

162
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:15,600
Don't do it!

163
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:20,620
I know the animosity you feel,

164
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:25,180
but your vengeance will only
sow the seeds of further violence.

165
00:11:25,500 --> 00:11:30,980
What you're doing is senseless revenge, and
it's feeding a fruitless cycle of death.

166
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:34,240
You must end this cycle once and for all.

167
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:36,100
Fullmetal Alchemist.

168
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,800
Fullmetal Alchemist.

169
00:11:42,200 --> 00:11:44,580
This girl is the doctors' daughter.?

170
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:48,020
You have the right.

171
00:11:48,020 --> 00:11:50,280
Shooting me would be justified.

172
00:11:56,860 --> 00:11:57,880
Brother!

173
00:11:58,500 --> 00:11:59,880
Brother!

174
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:02,100
Listen.

175
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:04,220
The armed forces have almost arrived.

176
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:06,500
This is no time to be
looking at your notes.

177
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:08,500
Just a minute more. I'm almost there.

178
00:12:09,880 --> 00:12:11,580
What are those tattoos for?

179
00:12:11,860 --> 00:12:13,220
Oh, these things?

180
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:18,500
The basis of alchemy is understanding
deconstruction, and reconstruction.

181
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:21,060
My right arm deconstructs.

182
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:23,280
My left arm reconstructs.

183
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:28,140
I studied the alkahestry they use in the
East and then added my own touches.

184
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:30,800
I discovered something else in my research.

185
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,760
The alchemy of this land is quite unusual.

186
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:36,280
None of that stuff matters anymore,
didn't you hear me?

187
00:12:36,300 --> 00:12:37,320
The army is here!

188
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:38,120
Stop.

189
00:12:41,020 --> 00:12:42,140
Why are you interfering?

190
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:43,780
We have to get away from here now!

191
00:12:43,780 --> 00:12:45,680
Please, calm down and listen.

192
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:50,180
Your brother's alchemy might be
the only way we have of saving Ishval.

193
00:12:50,500 --> 00:12:51,500
What?

194
00:12:51,820 --> 00:12:52,980
You must have heard.

195
00:12:53,180 --> 00:12:55,240
The enemy has State Alchemists.

196
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:56,500
They're weapons.

197
00:12:56,780 --> 00:13:00,440
Using their dirty magic to cut a path
of destruction through the country.

198
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:03,500
Even though we're
Amestrian citizens just like them.

199
00:13:04,340 --> 00:13:06,500
I've heard all about the military dogs.

200
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:09,980
But what do they have to do
with my brother's research?

201
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:13,780
Your brother is the only one who
can stand against the State Alchemists.

202
00:13:14,020 --> 00:13:18,420
If he can match their power with his,
he could find a way to annihilate the military.

203
00:13:18,420 --> 00:13:20,580
The threat to us would be ended!

204
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:24,940
Kill them before they can kill us.

205
00:13:24,940 --> 00:13:26,020
Take them down.

206
00:13:26,020 --> 00:13:28,120
With alchemy, we'll beat
them at their own game.

207
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:29,980
Pay them back in blood.

208
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:33,840
Do you see this, brother?

209
00:13:34,260 --> 00:13:36,940
This is the science that you
would spend your life following.

210
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:40,500
You may think it's for the greater good,
that it could help our people.

211
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:45,300
You don't even see
the evil you're creating!

212
00:13:48,580 --> 00:13:49,640
Run!

213
00:13:52,060 --> 00:13:56,320
[SCREAMS AND MARCHING]

214
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:21,940
So this is your alchemy, brother?

215
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:25,940
[LAUGHING]

216
00:14:33,360 --> 00:14:35,040
This is the great power?

217
00:14:35,060 --> 00:14:37,140
This is going to save our people?

218
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:55,000
This science causes nothing
but destruction and slaughter.

219
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:56,740
It can't save us.

220
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:03,400
Oh, no!

221
00:15:08,340 --> 00:15:10,660
Father! Mother!

222
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:13,000
Are you all right?

223
00:15:13,060 --> 00:15:14,480
Yes, we're both okay.

224
00:15:14,540 --> 00:15:18,100
Luckily, we were already prepared to flee
from here in case we needed to.

225
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:19,700
Sorry I'm late.

226
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:22,500
There were some important
notes I needed to compile.

227
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:23,880
What do you mean?

228
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:26,280
Here. I want you to hold on to this.

229
00:15:26,420 --> 00:15:27,720
Why? What is it?

230
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:29,500
These are my research notes.

231
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:31,540
This is all that I was able to bring.

232
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:33,300
Take them and get away now.

233
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:34,420
Hold on a minute—

234
00:15:34,420 --> 00:15:38,140
If anything happens to me, I don't want
my research to have been for nothing.

235
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:40,800
Why don't you just take
it and run away yourself?

236
00:15:41,060 --> 00:15:43,620
Because you're a warrior
of the Ishvalan people.

237
00:15:43,620 --> 00:15:45,060
You've been well trained.

238
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:47,000
Let's be honest here,

239
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,540
You're a lot more likely
to survive this than I am.

240
00:15:50,420 --> 00:15:51,580
Just look.

241
00:15:52,860 --> 00:15:54,500
My legs won't stop shaking.

242
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:57,580
Some big brother.

243
00:15:58,340 --> 00:15:59,700
You will survive.

244
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:06,900
Is that a soldier?

245
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:13,740
Look at his hands!

246
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:15,360
He's a State Alchemist!

247
00:16:27,260 --> 00:16:29,360
Get back!

248
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:34,880
Ahh!

249
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:52,440
Stay with me.

250
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:54,240
Don't you die.

251
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:00,680
Damn.

252
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:02,720
I can't stop the bleeding.

253
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:04,200
His arm...

254
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:06,640
Where's my brother's arm?

255
00:17:06,740 --> 00:17:08,400
Where is it?

256
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:11,620
Father...

257
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:13,760
Mother...

258
00:17:14,380 --> 00:17:15,700
Someone?

259
00:17:16,100 --> 00:17:17,540
Anyone?!

260
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:28,760
Don't die.

261
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:30,500
I won't let you.

262
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:36,060
I have to keep fighting.

263
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:37,860
Let me go back out there.

264
00:17:37,860 --> 00:17:39,800
No. You're staying right where you are.

265
00:17:39,840 --> 00:17:40,780
That's right.

266
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:42,860
We didn't treat you just to let you die.

267
00:17:42,980 --> 00:17:45,220
Doctor, you and your
wife should get out of here.

268
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:47,240
Young man, we're not going anywhere.

269
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:50,520
Brother...

270
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:52,860
Get back!

271
00:17:53,500 --> 00:17:54,960
What happened?

272
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:56,840
Why did you protect me?

273
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:59,580
Brother?

274
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:03,920
Anyone who can move on their own, go now.

275
00:18:05,780 --> 00:18:07,000
He's awake!

276
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:11,200
Don't move or you'll open up your wounds.

277
00:18:11,220 --> 00:18:12,340
Come here.

278
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:13,820
Dear, come here.

279
00:18:15,560 --> 00:18:18,240
You aren't well enough to
move around on your own yet.

280
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:20,420
Somebody, get a cart.

281
00:18:20,420 --> 00:18:21,820
Take this man with you.

282
00:18:21,820 --> 00:18:23,500
He needs help.

283
00:18:24,460 --> 00:18:26,580
Brother's tattoos...

284
00:18:27,280 --> 00:18:28,700
You're alive.

285
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:30,460
Brother, you've made it.

286
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:35,220
[GASP]

287
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:38,280
What is going on here?!

288
00:18:40,080 --> 00:18:41,160
Sedatives!

289
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:43,520
There aren't any more.
We used them all up!

290
00:18:51,100 --> 00:18:53,160
State Alchemist.

291
00:18:53,780 --> 00:18:56,020
Amestrians.

292
00:18:56,560 --> 00:18:58,600
You will pay.

293
00:18:58,600 --> 00:19:00,500
[CRASH]

294
00:19:01,980 --> 00:19:03,760
All of you.

295
00:19:03,980 --> 00:19:06,980
- All of you will pay...
- Doctor Rockbell!

296
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:09,360
[SCREAMS]

297
00:19:41,940 --> 00:19:43,600
Go on, shoot.

298
00:19:44,260 --> 00:19:45,580
Don't do it, Winry.

299
00:19:45,580 --> 00:19:46,660
Put down the gun.

300
00:19:46,700 --> 00:19:48,620
You know you don't wanna do this.

301
00:19:48,760 --> 00:19:49,740
Winry!

302
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:51,180
Shoot, girl.

303
00:19:51,220 --> 00:19:53,620
But know, the moment
you pull the trigger,

304
00:19:53,620 --> 00:19:56,020
There's no going back,
you will be my enemy.

305
00:19:56,020 --> 00:19:57,100
Scar!

306
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:59,880
If you think I'll let you hurt
one hair on her head—

307
00:19:59,880 --> 00:20:01,020
Will you kill me?

308
00:20:01,080 --> 00:20:02,500
That'd be fine with me.

309
00:20:02,940 --> 00:20:06,660
Until one of us dies, boy,
this chain of hatred will continue.

310
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:08,600
But don't ever forget!

311
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:10,760
Don't ever forget it was the Amestrians

312
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:13,060
who first pulled the
trigger during the Civil War.

313
00:20:13,260 --> 00:20:14,940
It was your people!

314
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:20,960
Winry, don't shoot.

315
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:23,500
Just put the gun down and get out of here.

316
00:20:24,100 --> 00:20:25,400
Winry!

317
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:29,760
If you can't shoot, then
do as the boy told you.

318
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,720
You're in my way.

319
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:38,000
Don't shoot!

320
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,000
Get back!

321
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:54,680
My brother...

322
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,240
Ed, you idiot, what are you doing?

323
00:21:11,340 --> 00:21:13,140
Both of you will get killed!

324
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:16,000
Hurry and get Winry somewhere safe.

325
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:26,000
Winry, let go of the gun.

326
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:28,500
I couldn't shoot.

327
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:30,580
I know you couldn't.

328
00:21:30,980 --> 00:21:32,340
And it's okay.

329
00:21:32,580 --> 00:21:33,960
But that man...

330
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:37,000
You said he's the one
who killed my mom and dad.

331
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:40,360
He tried to kill you and Al too, Ed.

332
00:21:40,740 --> 00:21:42,020
But I couldn't.

333
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:43,480
Why not?

334
00:21:45,300 --> 00:21:48,560
Remember in Rush Valley,
you delivered that baby?

335
00:21:48,620 --> 00:21:50,500
You saved two lives.

336
00:21:52,220 --> 00:21:58,280
And you gave me an arm and a leg,
to replace the ones I've lost.

337
00:22:00,140 --> 00:22:01,740
It's your hands.

338
00:22:02,460 --> 00:22:04,000
They weren't meant to kill.

339
00:22:05,420 --> 00:22:07,440
They're meant to give life.

340
00:22:09,300 --> 00:22:10,620
That's why.

341
00:22:15,280 --> 00:22:18,320
[SOBBING]

342
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:34,400
Let it all out, let it all out

343
00:22:34,400 --> 00:22:38,760
Tsuyogaranakute ii n da ne

344
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:45,100
Dareka ga kaite'tta

345
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:51,120
Kabe no rakugaki no hana ga yureru

346
00:22:51,580 --> 00:22:56,820
Jibunrashisa nante, dare mo wakaranai yo

347
00:22:56,820 --> 00:23:02,200
Nagai nagai michi no tochuu
de nakushitari, hirottari, 

348
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:11,960
Kyuu ni samishiku natte,
naichau hi mo aru kedo

349
00:23:12,160 --> 00:23:17,580
Namida mo itami mo, hoshi ni kaeyou

350
00:23:17,660 --> 00:23:23,840
Ashita wo terasu akari wo tomosou

351
00:23:23,840 --> 00:23:31,780
Chiisana te kazashite
futari de tsukurou hoshikuzu wo

352
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:34,040
Tsuyoku hikaru ein wo

353
00:23:34,040 --> 00:23:39,340
Sayonara itsuka wa kuru ka mo shirenu

354
00:23:39,340 --> 00:23:45,560
Kisetsu wa sore demo meguri megutte'ku

355
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:53,200
Chiisaku mayotte mo aruite'ku
Kimi to aruite'ku

356
00:23:53,280 --> 00:23:57,740
Sore daku wa kawaranaide iyou ne

357
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:03,900
What happens when someone must
give something up, in order to protect it?

358
00:24:04,320 --> 00:24:06,340
Will his resolve falter?

359
00:24:06,600 --> 00:24:09,600
Will he crumble beneath
the weight of sacrifice?

360
00:24:10,020 --> 00:24:14,980
Or will his heart remain strong,
ready to do whatever is necessary?

361
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:18,780
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

362
00:24:19,220 --> 00:24:23,220
Episode 23: Girl on the Battlefield

363
00:24:23,460 --> 00:24:25,940
You must not show any tears of sorrow.

364
00:24:37,500 --> 00:24:38,620
That is part of the promise.
